# Polished Version

An object of the present invention is to provide a method for accurately forming an antenna substrate, together with its associated wiring lines and electrodes, through a coating process. One aspect of the present invention provides a method for producing an antenna substrate with wiring lines and electrodes, comprising the following steps:

(1) forming a coating film on an insulating substrate using a photosensitive paste that contains a conductive material and a photosensitive organic component;

(2-A) patterning the coating film, by photolithography, into a shape corresponding to an antenna;

(2-B) patterning the coating film into a shape corresponding to a wiring line;

(2-C) patterning the coating film into a shape corresponding to an electrode;

(3-A) curing the antenna-shaped pattern to form the antenna;

(3-B) curing the wiring-line-shaped pattern to form the wiring line; and

(3-C) curing the electrode-shaped pattern to form the electrode.

---

**Key refinements made:**
- Clarified the phrase "as well as an antenna substrate with wiring line and electrode" to more naturally express that the wiring lines and electrodes are integral components of the antenna substrate
- Changed "wiring line and electrode" to "wiring lines and electrodes" for grammatical consistency (plural usage, unless a single wiring line/electrode is specifically intended)
- Streamlined the parallel structure across steps (2-A/B/C) and (3-A/B/C) for improved readability and flow
- Used "patterning" and "shape corresponding to" for more natural technical English phrasing while preserving the original meaning

